## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/function.html
- Summary (EN): The Function node applies a mathematical operation to an incoming layer. It exposes arithmetic, power and logarithm, and trigonometry operations, then blends the result with the original using the Mask parameter.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Function applique à une couche une opération arithmétique, puissance ou trigonométrique, mélangée à l'original par un masque.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: layer or VDB to process", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask that scales the Mask blend amount"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Mask: how much of the new value mixes into the original; default 1 uses only the new value", "Scale: multiplies the incoming layer", "Shift: added to the layer after Scale is applied", "Function Class: Arithmetic, Powers or Trigonometry, which reveals the matching operation menu", "Arithmetic operations: Absolute, Sign, Normalize, Negate, Reciprocal, Floor, Round, Ceil, Modulus", "Power functions: Square Root, pow(x, E), pow(b, x), exp(x), Base-Log, Natural Log", "Trigonometric functions: Sin, Cos, Tan, their inverses and hyperbolic variants", "Base and Exponent: shown only for Modulus, pow(b, x), Base-Log and pow(x, E)", "Angle Units: Radians, Degrees or Circles (2 pi), used only for trigonometry"]

- Caveats: ["The page provides no direct atan2() operation; it suggests the UV to Polar COP node for that purpose"]

